---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import SkillBlock from '../components/SkillBlock.astro';
import DemoPlayer from '../components/DemoPlayer.astro';
import KeepGoing from '../components/KeepGoing.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Conversational language · agent-toolkit"
  description="Texts that sound like a real human typed them, not sophisticated AI prose."
  back
>
  <PageHeader title="Conversational language" heading="Texts that sound like a real human typed them">
    <p class="text-muted">
      We often ask AI to help draft texts that other people will read: chat replies, PR comments,
      commit messages. The agent is great at drafting them quickly, but not at matching the tone
      to the context: a chat reply doesn't want the polish of a README, yet everything comes out
      in the same overly formal, fancy prose that readers recognize as AI at a glance.
    </p>
    <p class="text-muted mt-3">
      The skill and rule below take the best of both worlds: the agent's speed, your voice.
    </p>
  </PageHeader>
  <SkillBlock name="use-conversational-language" color="blue">
    <p class="text-muted mb-4">
      Tells the agent to write in simple, human language instead of sophisticated AI prose full
      of — em dashes — and fancy terms. It adapts the voice to the kind of text (a PR comment, a
      chat reply, a code comment) and changes the wording only, never the content: you still
      review every text before it goes out.
    </p>
    <DemoPlayer cast="07-explain-refactor" cols={72} rows={16} label="use-conversational-language rewriting a refactor explanation" />
  </SkillBlock>
  <SkillBlock name="write-realistic-texts" color="blue" rule>
    <p class="text-muted">
      Opt-in rule that applies the skill automatically whenever the agent writes something a
      human will read as if a person wrote it, even when writing wasn't the task you gave it.
    </p>
  </SkillBlock>
  <section class="px-6">
    <div class="max-w-page mx-auto border-t border-border py-8">
      <a class="more-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
        href="https://medium.com/engineering-in-the-age-of-ai/how-to-use-ai-to-generate-texts-that-sound-like-a-human-would-actually-write-them-c7eef78e0b42">
        Read more about the conversational voice &rarr;</a>
    </div>
  </section>
  <KeepGoing current="conversational-language" />
</Base>
